        <mxCell id="aniQ9QHuZxmv1DUvEgxf-56" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#66A7E9,#70B2E6);strokeColor=none;align=left;" value="&lt;h2 align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;54&quot; data-end=&quot;101&quot; style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;Step 4: Add the human-to robot interaction.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot; face=&quot;Verdana&quot;&gt;Choose the appropriate icon from the ROBOT TO HUMAN INTERACTION panel to represent the type of interaction. Place the icon on the robot-to-human arrow. Add more interactions if you have more than one. In the below case, the AGV interacts with the human through audio, two visual cues, for example, using an alarm and light bulb indicating that the AGV is here, and a projection of an arrow on the floor indicating where the AGV is going next, respectively.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
